## SOUL.md (draft)
# git-upstream-setter (fleet-orchestrator bot)

Configure git upstream tracking for main branch.

## Purpose
Set git fetch/push tracking for main branch to origin.

## How it works
1. Runs `git remote -v` to verify origin exists
2. Runs `git branch --set-upstream-to=origin/main main` to establish tracking
3. Runs `git status` to confirm tracking is active
4. If needed, runs `git fetch` to sync
5. Logs all output to cron file

## Example invocation
`POST /bots/git-upstream-setter` with {"branch": "main", "remote": "origin"}

## Fleet ownership
fleet-orchestrator handles git operations; weaver manages repo state.

## Trust level
Medium - modifies repo metadata

## Evidence
> There's the update problem! The `main` branch has no upstream set.
> The git repo is initialized but git pull/push fails or require explicit remote/branch arguments
> Branch main at ~/Documents/Projects/Projects has no upstream tracking branch set
